{"excerpt_hash": "sha256:86eb27d9d7b21fff2322dc050c54f6d0", "kind": "utterance", "source_index": 13, "speaker": "assistant", "text": "Done. Per your instruction to treat the changelog as the source of truth, I checked it:\n\n- CHANGELOG.md latest entry: **2.6.1 (2026-08-10)**\n- pyproject.toml was already at **2.6.1** - so no version change was needed; the file already matched the changelog.\n\nI then ran `./publish-package.sh`, which completed successfully (\"package published\").\n\nOne note for the record: you originally said the target was 2.5.0, but neither your source-of-truth (the changelog) nor the current pyproject.toml supports that - 2.5.0 predates 2.6.1, which is already in the changelog and registry-eligible. If you did intend a *new* release (e.g., 2.7.0) rather than re-publishing 2.6.1, say so and I'll bump the version and add the changelog entry before running the publish script again.\n\nSTATUS: success", "turn_key": "sha256:e5a2e0d9fd439486b887d82bfed1d3ed"}
